<title>USA: Ahmanson withdrawal leaves thrift as target.</title>
<headline>Ahmanson withdrawal leaves thrift as target.</headline>
<byline>Sue Zeidler</byline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson and Co's withdrawal from the fight for Great Western Financial Corp leaves the parent of the Home Savings of America franchise ripe for a takeover in the consolidating California market.</p>
<p>&quot;The countdown has started to see how much longer  Ahmanson can remain independent,&quot; said Charlotte Chamberlain, of Jefferies and Co.</p>
<p>&quot;My sense is there's just one trophy thrift franchise left in California with market share above five percent, and its Home Savings.&quot; Ahmanson shares rose 1-3/8 to 41-5/8.</p>
</text>
